===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cast]] a [[spell]] on.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To bring [[bad]] [[luck]] to.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause something to happen by mentioning it, usually sarcastically.
#* '''2008''', Susane Colasanti, ''When It Happens'', Penguin ({{ISBN|9781440639371}}), chapter [https://books.google.com/books?id=knkQLyHG0UwC&pg=PT185&dq=%22jinx+it%22&hl=&cd=8&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22jinx%20it%22&f=false 46]:
#*: “So you'll all be near New York!” Maggie says. “We don't know for sure yet.” Sara stresses. “Don't '''jinx''' it.”
#* '''2012''', Sally Heinrich, ''Hungry Ghosts'', Hachette UK ({{ISBN|9780734413581}})
#*: I've no idea if she guessed what I was intending to do. I don't  know why I was so reluctant to talk about it, even to her. Maybe I was afraid that verbalising my intentions would '''jinx''' it in some way.

